In a nested-checkbox round, the children's checked ids live in one `Set` in state. The parent checkbox must look checked only when every child is checked, look partially checked when some (but not all) are, and never be out of sync with the children, not even for one render.

```jsx
const [checkedIds, setCheckedIds] = useState(new Set());
// children: [{ id: 'a' }, { id: 'b' }, { id: 'c' }]
```

Which way of getting the parent's state meets every requirement?

